1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:06,520
Stock tokens look familiar. But a ticker and a good price don't tell you what you're buying.

2
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,620
This is KineGate, with synthetic narration.

3
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:14,270
You're seeing the actual product. These examples are fixtures.

4
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:17,540
The external API evidence is a recorded replay.

5
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:24,210
Start with fifty dollars. KineGate checks this exact issuer, amount, permission, and route,

6
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:25,710
before any action.

7
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:31,320
That decision gets a receipt. Every reviewed input is bound together.

8
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:34,870
Change the inputs, and the receipt no longer applies.

9
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:37,460
The local simulation is recorded once.

10
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,870
It sends nothing to the blockchain.

11
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:45,550
Now change the amount. The old receipt turns invalid.

12
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:48,160
We don't quietly manufacture another quote.

13
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:53,490
Over the weekend, the displayed price may be stale.

14
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:57,420
This case waits for fresh evidence, rather than trusting the gap.

15
00:00:58,950 --> 00:01:02,340
The same ticker can name a different issuer's claim.

16
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:04,970
Those rights can't be treated as interchangeable.

17
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:12,060
Time matters, too. Advance this virtual clock by a minute, and the receipt expires.

18
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:14,210
Fresh evidence is needed again.

19
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:19,020
We tested both approaches on the same sixteen fixtures.

20
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:22,320
The price-only shortcut missed thirteen unsafe cases.

21
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:24,200
KineGate blocked all thirteen.

22
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:29,180
Now the real integration evidence. Four recorded Binance calls succeeded.

23
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:33,980
The issuer and contract match. Missing execution evidence stays unresolved.

24
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,900
This six dollar quote was actually returned.

25
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:41,980
But it is historical evidence, not a current offer, or authorization to trade.

26
00:01:43,810 --> 00:01:47,710
The real off-chain simulation failed: insufficient balance.

27
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:52,160
The transaction was never approved, signed, or broadcast.

28
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:56,590
A pinned-block read confirms the token contract and its decimals.

29
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:59,510
That proves existence, not a settled trade.

30
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:02,790
Settlement is unverified. Signing needs permission.

31
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:05,610
A human must write the report.

32
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:11,640
Try it without a wallet. Inspect the receipts, tests, and limits.

33
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,500
KineGate. Evidence before action.
